{include:`layouts/auth.html.dtmpl`}
  {fill:content}
    <h1 class="h4 mb-4">Confirm your address</h1>

    {loop:flashes.error}
      <div class="alert alert-danger">{var:item.message}</div>
    {endloop}
    {loop:flashes.success}
      <div class="alert alert-success">{var:item.message}</div>
    {endloop}

    {unless:flashes.success}
      {comment}
        An identifier is confirmed or it is not used at all: an unconfirmed
        address cannot sign you in, cannot receive anything but this one message,
        and cannot recover the account. This page is where the confirming
        happens, and the state the account is in is said plainly above the form
        rather than left to be discovered -- a person who signs out before
        confirming cannot sign back in, and being told that afterwards is no
        use.

        The FORM is the Identity module's definition. The fields, the action,
        the CSRF id and the validation live in
        `config/modules/identity/forms/verify-email.yaml`; this page is the
        chrome around it. The mail links here with `?token=`, which the module
        fills into the code field.
      {endcomment}
      <p class="text-body-secondary">
        We sent a code to the address you registered with. Enter it here to
        confirm the address. Until it is confirmed it cannot be used to sign in
        or to recover the account.
      </p>

      {widget:form:`identity.verify_email`}

      <hr class="my-4">

      <p class="text-body-secondary small mb-2">
        No code, or has it expired? We will send another one.
      </p>
      {widget:form:`identity.verify_email_resend`}
    {endunless}

    <p class="mt-3 text-center">
      <a href="{var:routes.login}">Back to login</a>
    </p>
  {endfill}
{endinclude}
